	(text "BRAKE ACTUATOR. Every line from the pod has a 10 k pull-down here (R50-R53): with the pod in reset,\nunpowered or unplugged, the drive, enable and magnet lines read LOW: released, cable dropped free.\nU3 (74HCT244, TTL thresholds) turns the pod's 3.3 V logic into the 5 V the BTS7960 module expects."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "94e7c694-a7a6-4c90-aeed-fb5452a15dab")
	)
	(text "Actuator power comes ONLY through the 40 A kill relay's\ncontacts (J5), whose coil is fed through the E-stop.\nQ2 holds the cable magnet; D14 absorbs its turn-off spike."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 254.0 142.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "2ddc0841-8380-4ff2-a2da-8fbdf1c25385")
	)
	(text "ACS712-20A module: 2.5 V at 0 A, 100 mV/A.\nR47/R48 scale it by 2/3 so nothing above\n3.3 V travels up the cable to the pod's ADC."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 254.0 223.52 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "3139588a-55c7-4996-9ce9-ce6af05b152e")
	)
